(\textbf{b-possibly causal path, b-non-causal path})
Let $p = \langle X=V_0, \dots , V_k=Y \rangle$, $k \geq 1$ be a path from node $X$ to node $Y$ in a maximal $\mathrm{PDAG}${} $\g$. We say that $p$ is b-possibly causal in $\g$ if and only if no edge $V_{i} \leftarrow V_{j}, 0 \le i < j \le k$ is in $\g$. Otherwise, we say that $p$ is b-non-causal path in $\g$.
\label{def:posdir-path}

$(b-PossDe(\mathbf{X},\g) \text{ and }b-PossAn(\mathbf{X},\g))$
Let $\textbf{X}$ be a node set in a maximal $\mathrm{PDAG}${} $\g$. Then $W$ is a b-possible descendant (b-possible ancestor) of $\mathbf{X}$ in $\g$, and we write $W \in b-PossDe(\mathbf{X},\g)$ $(W \in b-PossAn(\mathbf{X},\g))$ if and only if $W \in \mathbf{X}$ or there is a node $X \in \mathbf{X}$ and a b-possibly causal path from $X$ to $W$ ($W$ to $X$) in $\g$.
\label{def:posde-1}

{(\textbf{Adjustment set})}
   Let $\mathbf{X,Y}$ and $\mathbf{Z}$ be pairwise disjoint node sets in a causal maximal $\mathrm{PDAG}${} $\g$. Then $\mathbf{Z}$ is an adjustment set relative to $(\mathbf{X,Y})$ in~$\g$ if for any density $f$ consistent with $\g$ we have
   \begin{equation}
   f(\mathbf{y}|do(\mathbf{x}))=
   \begin{cases}
   f(\mathbf{y}|\mathbf{x}) & \text{if }\mathbf{Z} = \emptyset,\\
   \int_{\mathbf{z}}f(\mathbf{y}|\mathbf{x,z})f(\mathbf{z})d\mathbf{z}  & \text{otherwise.}
   \end{cases}
   \nonumber
   \end{equation}
   \label{defadjustmentmpdag}

